//
// A value written through a `&` link or a `&` parameter is stored into the linked slot
// (`binding.md (B-Ref-Uniform)`), so a store that is not provably inside a narrow slot's range is
// refused at compile time with the cure named (`types.md (I-Narrow)`), exactly as `w = w + 10`
// into the `u8` itself is.  Before loft#1604 each of these compiled and stored the unchecked
// value on both backends.
//
// Cells: a local link and a `&` parameter; `u8`, `i8` and a user `limit(1, 8)`.  Every expected
// error below is matched exactly once, so a second error for one write fails the file.  The
// compound spelling (`+=`) is not a refusal — it takes the slot's default — and has its own
// guard, `1604-a-compound-step-through-a-narrow-link-takes-the-slot-default.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: 73ae78232 — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/4 -> 0/4 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/4 -> 0/4 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
// @falsified-by: tests/falsified/1604-a-narrowing-write-through-a-link-is-refused.patch — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/4 -> 0/4 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/4 -> 0/4 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
// HOLDS: leak, panic and free-refusal are clean on both trees and both backends.
//
// CHANNEL: the expected diagnostics, one per refused write.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to u8 (may lose data)
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to u8 (may lose data)
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to i8 (may lose data)
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to integer(1, 8) (may lose data)

type Small = integer limit(1, 8);

fn bump(x: &u8) { x = x + 10; }
fn local_link() { w: u8 = 250; d = &w; d = d + 10; }
fn i8_parameter(y: &i8) { y = y * 2; }
fn small_link() { k: Small = 2; kk = &k; kk = kk * 50; }

fn main() {
  z: u8 = 250;
  bump(z);
  local_link();
  n: i8 = 100;
  i8_parameter(n);
  small_link();
}
